In the section "Scanned OCR Receipts (ERCA Cash Register Invoices)", add a duplicate check before building the matrix.

DUPLICATE RULE
A receipt is a duplicate of another if BOTH of these are identical:
1. FS No. (fiscal receipt number)
2. Seller TIN

If only one of the two matches, it is NOT a duplicate. Keep both receipts.

HOW TO COMPARE
- Normalize before comparing: trim spaces, remove dashes and special characters, ignore case, and remove leading zeros from the FS No. (OCR often adds or drops these).
- Compare every receipt against all other receipts in this section only.

WHICH ONE TO KEEP
- When a duplicate group is found (same FS No. + same Seller TIN), keep only ONE receipt, the LATEST one.
- "Latest" = the most recent receipt date and time. If the date and time are identical or missing, use the most recently scanned/uploaded one.
- Exclude the older duplicates from the matrix and from all totals so nothing is double-counted.

OUTPUT
1. The cleaned matrix, with one row per unique receipt.
2. A "Duplicates Removed" table with these columns:
   FS No. | Seller TIN | Kept Receipt (date/ref) | Removed Receipt(s) (date/ref) | Reason
3. A summary: total receipts scanned, duplicates removed, unique receipts used.

FLAG, DON'T GUESS
If an FS No. or Seller TIN is unreadable or missing from the OCR, do not treat the receipt as a duplicate. Keep it and flag it as "Needs manual review".